/-!
# Literal radius-two paid interval endpoints on the 144-bit grid

This finite table is a signed interval on 64 physical head coordinates and
one scalar-pole coordinate. Its exact endpoint JSON SHA-256 is
`bb7d222f6569f40fc51ec8b54e5a5ba43dc23d13e4b5d0f5b4970174a3c8236b`.
The exact-arithmetic extraction provenance SHA-256 is
`06dc55ef1524a95493c489cd136b6f380e56eb6deff5551e4568a9a8cf1ff5cd`;
its all-endpoint integer kernel pilot receipt SHA-256 is
`1ce43a3d6258e0d782e983cd2c88b3a62411cf920faaf640b54a02b13054a5e6`.
The packet compared against is the separately maintained
`RadiusTwoRankFourPaidPacket.bounds`; its own exact inputs and sign proof
are retained in `WeilRadiusTwoRankFourPaidData` and `AllRows`.

The two source endpoint numerators have denominator `2^144` and use biased
160-bit digits. The existing packet endpoint numerators have denominator
`2^108` and use biased 116-bit digits. Multiplication by exactly `2^36`
therefore brings a packet numerator to the same integer grid. Every one
of the 65-by-65 pairs is checked in both endpoint directions: 8450 integer
inequalities. Each cell also checks sourceLower ≤ sourceUpper, adding4225
interval-validity checks and preventing empty-interval vacuity. Four-row
proof modules retain bounded evaluation. An earlier
monolithic pilot reached its declared memory threshold; its failure is
not mathematical evidence against these inequalities.

The literal table was obtained from the new rank-four observed-grid recipe
with the 44-bit retained head and 45-bit raw rectangle. Its physical shift
is `-1/2`, while the scalar pole retains unshifted `1/2`. This records
provenance, not a proved source identity. Equality with the typed
`symmetricBounds (paidBounds ...)` remains OPEN. In particular, the checked
integer comparisons alone are not the actual `hCover` proposition.
The chosen new-reconstruction remote source enclosure and independent
`1/5` high floor at N=64 remain OPEN. No whole-window source paid sign,
cofinal family, RH or GRH follows from this file.

The actual finite claim compares these literal intervals with the already
checked packet. The aggregate rational consumer proves interval containment
and transfers its finite sign to any real matrix enclosed by these literal
intervals. Automated assistance supplied extraction and proof construction.
Independent analytical review: NOT_RUN. Novelty: NOT_ASSESSED. Formal
assurance is separate source-bound evidence recorded by Noe.
-/
